Add file attachments as referenceable assets (Option A)

The owner can attach images and PDFs in the chat. Files go to a public
site-assets bucket, are recorded in admin_uploads, and the assistant is told
their names and URLs so it can reference them -- "use this as the blog cover
image" -- via a new list_assets tool.

Deliberately NOT included: the assistant cannot see inside these files. Nothing
here gives the model any ability to interpret an image, so it is told to say
plainly that it cannot view photos. Reading a screenshot's contents is Option B
and needs a vision model plus its own safety pass, because text inside an image
is another injection surface.

- New migration: bucket, storage policies (public read, admin-only write and
  delete), and the admin_uploads table with RLS gated on is_admin().
- lib/uploads.ts validates type and size, generates a safe unique object path
  rather than trusting the uploaded filename, and reports metadata-save failures
  honestly instead of claiming the whole operation succeeded.
- Attachments are described to the assistant as plain text appended to the
  message, marked as referenceable-but-not-readable.
- UI: paperclip button, image thumbnails, per-file removal, and an
  attachment-only message is valid so a file can be handed over for later use.
- Limits: 8 MB, images and PDF only.
